 ],
 "literal": "He who does not see, he who shows, himself will not see; he who does not see, he who has seen becomes, the way he himself has seen.",
 "translation": "He who tries to teach a man who cannot see will himself fail to see. The man who cannot see will think he has seen, but only in his own limited way.",
 "modern": "அறிவில்லாதவனுக்கு அறிவுரை கூற முயல்பவன், தானும் அறிவில்லாதவன் ஆவான். அந்த அறிவில்லாதவனோ, தனக்குத் தெரிந்த அளவிலேயே தான் எல்லாம் அறிந்தவனாக நினைத்துக்கொள்வான்.",
